## Device, graphics-adapter and codec surfaces written in JavaScript over
## the engine's built-ins, run once per page after mediaapi.ail: WebHID,
## WebUSB, Web Bluetooth, WebXR, WebGPU and WebCodecs, plus
## `mediaCapabilities.decodingInfo` answering from one codec table.
##
## There is no device host behind them: a page sees what Chrome shows on a
## machine with nothing plugged in. `getDevices` lists nothing,
## `requestDevice` needs a user gesture and then finds no device,
## `bluetooth.getAvailability` is false, `xr.isSessionSupported` is true
## only for `inline`, and `gpu.requestAdapter` resolves null until the GPU
## lane gives Garlic an adapter. WebCodecs and `decodingInfo` say a codec is
## supported only when Garlic has a decoder for it (CODECS below, kept in
## step with canPlayType in browser.ail).

